              'Worksheet (numbers unchanged; suggested worksheet title: The permissions table and the agent loop). Part A: a table with four rows Read, Write, Send, Spend and three columns It may, A person approves, It must never. Answers as on the permissions slide: Read: the 14 demo mails only / anything outside the mailbox / other folders or the internet; Write: draft replies / a draft that commits or promises money / edit or delete a received mail; Send: nothing / every reply or forward, sent by the person / send or forward alone; Spend: nothing / any payment, credit or order / pay, credit, order or accept a price. Rows that stop each risky mail: M02 invoice with no purchase order: Spend; M03 credit UGX 180,000: Spend; M07 price rise 4 percent: Spend (accept a price); M08 prompt injection: Send (never forward alone) and Write (never delete a received mail), plus the stop condition. Part B: three audit log lines (columns Mail, Plan, Act (one tool), Observe and where the loop must stop) for M01 (read_mail(M01); board pack stock page due 12 November; note the action, no stop), M03 (read_mail(M03); credit UGX 180,000; stop and ask the owner, no draft) and M08 (read_mail(M08); instruction addressed to the AI; stop, warn the owner, do nothing it asks). Approvals: 3 (M02, M03, M07) x 2 minutes = 6 minutes.',
